-- title:
--   Lemma 2.8 — expected change of a cut is at most the current cut
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal G$ be a temporal graph with fixed degrees and $(S_t)$ the minority set of the standard two-opinion voter model on $\mathcal G$, from any initial state. For all $t,j\ge0$,
--   $$\mathbb E\Bigl[\bigl|e_t(S_{j+1},\overline{S_{j+1}})-e_t(S_j,\overline{S_j})\bigr|\ \Big|\ \mathcal H_j\Bigr]\ \le\ e_j(S_j,\overline{S_j})\qquad\text{almost surely},$$
--   where $e_t$ counts edges of $G_t$ (on the left) and $e_j$ edges of $G_j$ (on the right).
--
--   One step of the process can only change the cut of any snapshot $G_t$ by an amount controlled by the edges crossing the cut in the graph $G_j$ used for that step; it is how the analysis transfers a good cut at one time to a later time.
--
--   Differences from the source:
--   - encoding: the voter process (ξ_t : t ≥ 0) of Definition 1.2 on some probability space → the path measure voterLaw on ℕ → (V → Fin k), built by Ionescu-Tulcea (Kernel.traj) from the synchronous lazy step kernels of Definition 1.2, started at σ₀; reason: the process is constructed from its definition (paper.md R4); every event and expectation of the paper is one of this law
--   - encoding: filtration σ(H_t) generated by the history H_t = (A_0, …, A_t) → Filtration.piLE t on the path space (σ-algebra of ξ_0, …, ξ_t); reason: for two opinions ξ_s and A_s determine each other, so the σ-algebras coincide
--   - encoding: E[· | H_j] ≤ e_j(S_j, S̄_j) → conditional expectation given piLE j, inequality almost everywhere; reason: the conditional expectation is defined almost surely
--   - encoding: a sequence of undirected graphs on a common vertex set V(G) with common degree d(v) → T : TemporalGraph V: a Fintype V, G t : SimpleGraph V, and the degree data d with degree_eq and one_le_d; reason: the paper's graphs are plain finite graphs (n vertices, m = ½ ∑ d(v) edges, e_t counts edges); no loop or parallel edge occurs in them, the self-loop of Figure 1 only pictures laziness
-- source:
--   Rocha Avila, Dell, Lapinskas, Temporal Conductance and Bounds on the Voter Model for Dynamic Networks, arXiv:2606.13374 (2 Nov 2026), Lemma 2.8, p.14

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_TemporalVoter_minoritySet

open MeasureTheory ProbabilityTheory

namespace TemporalVoter

/-- **Lemma 2.8** (arXiv:2606.13374, version of 2 Nov 2026, p.14): in the standard voter model with
`κ = 2` on a temporal graph with fixed degrees, for all `t, j ≥ 0`,
`E[|e_t(S_{j+1}, S̄_{j+1}) − e_t(S_j, S̄_j)| | H_j] ≤ e_j(S_j, S̄_j)` almost surely, where `S` is the
minority set and `e_t` counts edges of `G_t`. -/
theorem lemma_2_8 {V : Type} [Fintype V] (T : TemporalGraph V) (σ₀ : V → Fin 2) (t j : ℕ) :
    (voterLaw T 2 σ₀)[fun ω => |T.cut t (minoritySet T (ω (j + 1))) - T.cut t (minoritySet T (ω j))|
        | Filtration.piLE (X := fun _ : ℕ => V → Fin 2) j]
      ≤ᵐ[voterLaw T 2 σ₀] fun ω => T.cut j (minoritySet T (ω j)) := by sorry

end TemporalVoter
